{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/47394-mummy-power-structures-in-cities","id":47394,"title":"Mummy power structures in cities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-12T08:13:40-08:00","id":47394,"title":"Mummy power structures in cities","content":"I am looking forward to the DC citybook for mummy because I am curious to see how mummies maintain power structures. The reason why is that, unlike vampires, mummies spend a long time in storage. Even though PC mummies can go through multiple calls to keep the game going, the default seems to be that most mummies only receive the call every few decades or centuries. This would indicate that power structures are mostly frozen in time in a status quo and only change over long periods because a mummy wakes up and makes some noise. Given the inactive nature of mummies, how do you think they gain and maintain power over long periods of time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T08:19:11-08:00","id":47398,"title":"","content":"Actually, their power structures would shift and evolve due to the motions of their cults. They are the primary actors most of the time, not the mummies themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T08:25:20-08:00","id":47402,"title":"","content":"That makes sense. So the cults would be responsible for maintaining power 99% of the time while the mummy is in storage. Power plays would then be a shadow war among cults with the occasional flare up when a mummy gets summoned","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T18:45:57-08:00","id":47793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/47394-mummy-power-structures-in-cities?p=47402#post47402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Power plays would then be a shadow war among cults with the occasional flare up when a mummy gets summoned</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I like the sound of that. Sothic cycles are really crazy, too, because there are dozens of Mummies waking up all over the place.<br /> <br /> Imagine a business office where only one or two guys show up to work at a time and even then they don't show up every day. Now what happens when half a dozen show up? And what happens when, every few years, there's a meeting where <i>all</i> employees show up and there's a near-guarantee of someone getting a promotion, transfer, or fired? I think that's the gist of it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T19:43:09-08:00","id":47814,"title":"","content":"From reading the core and Guildhalls, it seems that mummies aren't concerned with amassing power in any sort of time scale. Mummies sense of time is very different from our own. They wake up in a huge conflict between powerful sides, fall asleep, wake up and it's resolved. They've also been around for thousands of years and they would be a very stupid mummy not to try and amass some fortune or resources during that time. A mummy should also trust that its cult should be able to at least hold onto some power over the years. Especially if they have a corporation that's been around for decades (though not necessarily in the same form). It's basically, as long as I have the resources I need to function it's all good. That's why it's upon the cults to use the mummies power and influence to build something greater. Hell improving upon your gods empire is going to get you some big brownie points...if he remembers who you are that is. They can do that by gathering allies, amassing wealth through deals and hostile takeovers, or even finding a relic. Remember, this immortal being is your god. Someone you worship and love dearly (even if you've never seen her in person). The legend and the power pushes you to make the best of your situation, and maybe you can move up to the high priest of your cult. The power and the wealth at your fingertips. Who wouldn't work for that?<br /> <br /> However, as made apparent many times in the books, some mummies can be vindictive. They hold grudges and crave power. These are the mummies you have to watch out for. If one comes into your territory, it's going to end with conflict of some sort. Your cult is going to be attacked, your territory ransacked, and maybe some key relics stolen. There are cults that feel invincible because they have the power of a relic or they feel like their mummy will solve any problem. But those cults can be squashed with enough time and planning. A mummy is another matter.<br /> <br /> They're immortal just like you and what if they have more power? Do you run and save your cult and tomb? Or do you fight the battle so you don't look weak in the eyes of your cult and other mummies? And these battles can span decades between the two factions. Cults carrying out covert ops, political back and forth between mummy allies, or even fights using business and wealth. A fight between mummies can be a complex war on multiple fronts and who knows when it will ever end or how? The two mummies might just forget and move their cults onto another focus. Or the mummy might be rendered inert after losing her cult and everything. Or maybe it ends in peace and both are weaker but alive in the long run. A battle over territory is never short and never easy because you're dealing with immortals, they have all the time in the world and the power of gods.<br /> <br /> That felt very rambley...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T14:49:46-08:00","id":49301,"title":"","content":"The take I'm running with in my Mummy game is as follows...<br /> <br /> Most Mummies spend most of their time around Memory 3. This means that their clearest memories are of their lives in Irem and of their previous Descent. So their actions and societies are based on stagnant memories of their origins and recent events whose causes are lost to them. In the absence of any kind of personal memory, these immortals are all about <i>institutionalizing</i> their knowledge, encoding their own missions and agendas in their cults and Guilds. Movement within the structure of Guilds is possible - after all, your fellows will remember you being promoted or cast out, or interactions on that basis - but the reasons for the &quot;present&quot; structure will often be lost or obscured. Those Mummies with higher Memory have a dangerous advantage here, as they're able to better manipulate this institutional memory for their agenda, or the agenda of their cult or Judge.<br /> <br /> Outside of a Sothic Turn, the chances of two Mummies randomly awaking at the same time are miniscule. But it's pretty easy for a cult to awaken a Mummy if they've got a Relic or Vestige on hand. So I've decided that &quot;Nomes&quot; are grand conspiracies of nominally-allied Mummies linked together by networks of cults. The secret societies that support them share enough symbolism / belief / practice / what-have-you that they tend to call up their Mummies under roughly the same circumstances, and a Mummy who needs an ally who isn't awake has their &quot;phone number&quot;, so to speak - they can find their cult and work through the right protocols to wake their Nome-patriot for aid, judgment, teaching, or what-have-you. Even if the cult doesn't have a relic they can use, weak or poorly-aligned Vestiges aren't too rare, so they make a good &quot;calling card&quot;. Beneath this are &quot;Merets&quot;, Mummies with closer alliances, either due to personal feeling, memories of Irem, or especially well-aligned cults.<br /> <br /> In my framework, conflicts between Mummies tend to be transitory (over Relics, for example), personal (I hate B'oboth with the unreasoning fury of ten thousand years), religious (specifically, over Judges), or structural (as above, but also including &quot;my cult hates your cult&quot; and other such things).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T17:22:18-08:00","id":50268,"title":"","content":"So as a related question to help my understanding of this topic: Do you think Mummy is more designed to play as mostly Cult Members with one or a few Mummies? Or Everyone as a Mummy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T19:35:55-08:00","id":50346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/47394-mummy-power-structures-in-cities?p=50268#post50268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So as a related question to help my understanding of this topic: Do you think Mummy is more designed to play as mostly Cult Members with one or a few Mummies? Or Everyone as a Mummy?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is designed with both options in mind explicitly, and both play styles are detailed in different ways in the ST book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T11:29:29-08:00","id":50877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/47394-mummy-power-structures-in-cities?p=50346#post50346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is designed with both options in mind explicitly, and both play styles are detailed in different ways in the ST book.</div> </div> </div> </div>100% agreed. My game is of the &quot;everyone is a Mummy&quot; variety, but with the powers available to Mummies, Mummy + cultists seems totally viable. You could even have other players as a Mummy's Lifeless servitors or as Lucid Dead - ghosts who get full character sheets, and can be created and enhanced by a variety of Utterances.<br /> <br /> Lucid Dead are particularly fun, as they're nominally every bit as immortal as a Mummy, and open up a lot of cool stuff in the Underworld and Twilight, and crossover potential with Geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T11:53:09-08:00","id":50903,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, Then I think I'll go for the Mummy+Cultist model when I run it unless my players dislike that Idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T19:33:52-08:00","id":51304,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's always best to figure out what the players' preferences are in this. Mummy requires a certain level of negotiation and trust between the ST and the players, more than most World of Darkness games, due to the mechanics of Memory and issues such as this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T01:17:27-08:00","id":52212,"title":"","content":"It really can go both ways. One of my players explicitly enjoyed playing the cultists moreso than the Mummy itself. As the Mummy's memory developed, I found myself sort of creating an image in the Mummy's head of Reincarnation mixed with a Touchstone a la Vampire. His main cultists have an Archetype, sort of.. and that carries over into Memories, for him to have an anchor in them. I have yet to explicitly reveal if it is actually reincarnation, or just the Mummy forcing its own patterns and vision onto people to keep its memories alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}